    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are leaning heavily on top-of-the-order speed today to combat a slate of middling opposing arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.42) is our strongest play, bolstered by a prime leadoff spot and a dynamic platoon advantage against Dotel that keeps his efficiency ceiling high despite a respectable opponent xERA. Close behind him, **Josh Smith** (64.66) benefits from a significant 14% boost via dynamic platoon metrics against Bassitt; his ability to exploit this matchup makes him a vital start in the outfield. While **Caleb Durbin** (63.67) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (62.05) face moderate-to-high xERA matchups, both remain high-efficiency anchors due to their situational stability, providing essential floor support for our SB-starved Roto hunt.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench was **Chase Meidroth** (54.14). He narrowly missed the cut because, despite a favorable leadoff assignment, his total utility is currently eclipsed by the platoon-adjusted projections of **Junior Caminero** and **Colt Keith**. We are also keeping a cautious eye on **Trea Turner** (52.66); facing an elite arm like Sale (2.81 xERA) suppresses his ceiling considerably, though his high batting order position keeps him in the lineup despite the tough matchup. We have successfully avoided the sub-40 trap with **Dillon Dingler** (39.24), who is firmly benched to preserve game caps, and **Yordan Alvarez** remains sidelined, necessitating continued reliance on our current active OF depth of **Hector Rodriguez** and **Carson Benge** to manage the volume.",
